// `@IMG-001` (whole-image-or-null, and the addressing rule), `@IMG-002` (every
// colour type arrives as RGBA), `@IMG-003` (replacing a pixel, and why the local
// you read one into is a view of its slot rather than a snapshot) and `@IMG-004`
// (the range that is not a clamp, above).
